From: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:06:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add RDNA Wave Split-K FP8 support

- Add a wave32 rocWMMA path for skinny FP8
  matrix multiplication.
- Decode gfx1100 E4M3FN inputs to FP16 before
  FP16-to-FP32 WMMA accumulation.
- Use native FP8-to-FP32 WMMA on gfx1200 and
  gfx1201.
- Select wave32 or wave64 launches at runtime.
- Preserve and retest the existing gfx90a path.
- Add focused RDNA correctness validation.

Tools used:
- GPT-5.6 Sol: gpt-5.6-sol-high

Signed-off-by: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
